			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Fix extension activation and SCM provider integration\n\nKey fixes for extension activation and SCM functionality:\n\n1. **Configuration re-merge after extension scan** (AppLifecycle.rs):\n   - First-pass config merge ran before extensions were scanned, so\n     `contributes.configuration.properties[*].default` values weren't\n     available. `getConfiguration('git').get('enabled')` returned\n     undefined, causing vscode.git to short-circuit in `_activate` and\n     the SCM viewlet to stay empty.\n   - Add second-pass merge after extension scan to collect and apply\n     extension default configurations (113 extensions declare defaults).\n\n2. **Debug session lifecycle events** (DebugProvider.rs):\n   - Add `$onDidStartDebugSession` notification to Cocoon for extension\n     listeners, plus `sky://debug/sessionStart` emit for Sky.\n   - Fix termination payload to include `id` field for proper session\n     tracking, add `sky://debug/sessionEnd` emit.\n\n3. **SCM provider handle alignment** (RegisterScmProvider.rs):\n   - Cocoon uses sequential handles from `ScmNamespace.ts`, but Mountain\n     was computing DJB hash of scmId. Resource group updates arrived with\n     the sequential handle while providers were registered under the hash,\n     starving the SCM viewlet.\n   - Now reads `handle` / `scm_handle` from the wire payload verbatim,\n     falls back to hash only when absent.\n\n4. **SCM group update parsing** (UpdateScmGroup.rs):\n   - Wire format sends `scm_handle` + `group_handle` (\"<handle>/<groupId>\"),\n     not the flat `provider_id`/`group_id` the previous decoder expected.\n   - Split `group_handle` to extract groupId for renderer payload.\n\n5. **Output channel log routing** (OutputChannelAppend.rs):\n   - vscode.git \"Git\" channel logs are critical for diagnosing F6\n     silent-bail (extension activates but never reaches\n     `createSourceControl`). Route to `grpc` level instead of\n     `output-verbose`.\n\nAlso: minor formatting cleanup across 70+ files, documentation improvements.",
			"SHA": "190e8d070ed1277c1849075703fd20b34301a891"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-26T10:38:38Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				874,
				4
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Fix extension config loading and enhance search provider\n\nThe configuration loading code was searching for a VS Code manifest shape (`[{key, value}]` array) that doesn't exist in any real extension. Every `workspace.getConfiguration('foo')` lookup fell through to undefined, causing extensions like vscode.git to activate but never reach `createSourceControl()`.\n\nThe fix walks both the array AND object shapes that `contributes.configuration` accepts, extracts `default` values from each property schema, and inserts them into nested maps using dotted keys (e.g. `git.enabled` → `{\"git\": {\"enabled\": true}}`).\n\nSearchProvider receives major improvements:\n- Add `ColumnRange` tracking so the Sky renderer underlines actual match positions instead of whole lines\n- Fix line numbers: previously returned 0 (treated as \"no line info\"), now returns 1-based\n- Add byte→char map with binary search for O(log n) UTF-8 column lookups (previously O(n) per match, causing quadratic slowdown on match-dense files)\n- Cap preview length at 512 chars to avoid massive row layouts on minified files\n- Add per-line match cap (100) to prevent hangs on pathological regexes like `.` against long lines\n\nAlso switch TreeView error logging to the DebugOnce pattern to avoid flooding dev logs with repeated failures from the same view.",
			"SHA": "44bf29d434cdf1eac0409fe5e471383dd064a387"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-26T09:50:10Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				874,
				1
			],
			"Message": "perf(Mountain): Deduplicate dev log entries for unregistered commands\n\nReplace dev_log! macro with DebugOnce for unregistered view-action and workbench-internal commands. These commands fire repeatedly (view-action buttons clicked multiple times, getTelemetrySenderObject fires 30+ times per boot extension activation), causing N-line log trails that obscure other diagnostic output.\n\nThe new implementation uses a dedup key format (e.g., \"view-action-noop:{CommandId}\") so the first invocation still logs for debugging probe shape, while subsequent calls to the same command ID are silently suppressed.\n\nThis reduces dev log noise in hot IPC paths while preserving diagnostic value for identifying unregistered command patterns.",
			"SHA": "2120ad5e42aec918ce1f2bb0a769dd02a7cf2e84"
		},
